  "result": "**Module:** `test/orders.js` — order math for a small shop. `calcTotal` sums price×qty; `applyDiscount` applies SAVE10/SAVE20 percent codes; `averageItemPrice` = total/count; `formatOrder` renders line items + discounted total.\n\n**Bugs:**\n1. `calcTotal:5` — off-by-one: `i <= items.length` reads `items[items.length]` (undefined) → `TypeError` on `.price`. Use `i < items.length`.\n2. `averageItemPrice:20` — divides by `items.length` with no empty-array guard → `NaN` (and crashes anyway via bug 1). Return 0 when empty.\n3. Minor: `formatOrder`/`averageItemPrice` assume `items` non-empty and well-formed; no validation of `price`/`qty` types.\n\nFix for bug 1 (the crashing one):\n\n`orders.js:5` → `for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++)`",
